the nintendo switch may have been the  old guy in the room this year when  compared to the ps5 and xbox series x  but the switch arguably stole the show  when it came to exclusive games in 2021  it's approaching its fifth birthday and  nintendo has shown no signs of slowing  down on its avalanche of games you can  only play on the hybrid console given  all of the standout exclusives that  landed on the switch this year it was  difficult to whittle down the list to  the best of the best but that's exactly  what's happened here here are gamespot's  picks for the 5 best nintendo switch  exclusives of 2021  metroid dread was the biggest surprise  of the year for the nintendo switch to  be clear it's not surprising that it's  great it's just kind of wild that it  exists at all nintendo tasked mercury  steam with unburying metroid dread it  cancelled nintendo ds project from its  grave nearly two decades after the last  brand new side-scrolling metroid  adventure was released while fans  continued to wait for metroid prime 4  dredd offered a welcome return to  side-scrolling action that many nintendo  fans grew up on metroid dread hit all  the right notes balancing open-ended  exploration with exciting boss battles  and tight platforming sequences dread  simply felt incredible in motion whether  you were roaming the varied locales in  search of missile packs or taking on  your old buddy crade in a fight to the  death while dread followed the familiar  metroid progression it added some new  wrinkles such as the emmy or killer  robots that samus had to evade brand new  suit powers and more hidden areas than  ever before metroid dread brought  samus's winding story arc to a fitting  and immensely satisfying conclusion in  our metroid dread review stephen petit  wrote more than anything else metroid  dread feels like going back to a place  of comfort after a long time away though  the gameplay is refined and new features  have been added to the mix dread sticks  closely to the formula of its  predecessors in the end for longtime  fans like myself that's probably for the  best  there's nothing to dread here we're home  again  while nintendo switch owners didn't have  the chance to play the monster hunter  game that catapulted the franchise to  mega stardom capcom more than made up  for that with monster hunter rise  arguably even more dynamic than monster  hunter world ryze added a wonderful new  mechanic that completely altered the  flow of both combat and exploration the  wire bug essentially a grappling hook  let hunters zip around the richly  detailed locales in a flash and made  showdowns with the larger-than-life  monsters more versatile in addition to  the wire bug ryze introduced the ability  to ride palomutes across the maps to  speed up the pace and get you into the  thick of the action quicker in this  respect monster hunter ryze felt more  action-packed by removing the tedium and  letting you focus on what monster hunter  is all about make no mistake monster  hunter ryze still offered a layered  action rpg experience featuring more  than a dozen weapons with unique styles  to master loads of customization  features and increasingly challenging  hunts to test your skills this time  round though monster hunter felt more  approachable than ever before the switch  console exclusive earned a 9 out of 10.  richard wakeling wrote going toe to toe  with these intimidating beasts is the  unmistakable core of the monster hunter  experience and ryze still feels like he  distinctly monster hunter game even if  it's more of a fully fledged action  title than any other entry in the series  this renewed focus doesn't diminish its  layered rpg mechanics nor does it dumb  down on any single aspect of the hunt  certain changes make ryze a more  approachable game for newcomers but you  also have the freedom to tailor the  experience to your liking  pokemon snap for nintendo 64 has long  been one of the most beloved pokemon  spin-offs more than 20 years after its  release nintendo finally brought it back  though the title is rather uninspired  new pokemon snap marked a triumphant and  charming return for the on rails shooter  a more tranquil pokemon experience new  pokemon snap let fans observe pokemon in  their natural habitats just like the  original and collecting research data  for the professor proved to be a  relaxing joy filled with surprises and  callbacks to the original game developer  bandai namco did a wonderful job with  the levels packing them with vibrant  colors and intricacies that brought the  world to life new pokemon snap also had  far more to offer than the original  thanks to a wide array of objectives to  complete that made replaying the dynamic  stages well worth your time adding the  ability to edit your photos to your  liking and create albums was a nice  touch and the sheer variety of pokemon  roaming the world nudged us to fill out  our collection much like our pokedex in  the mainline games in our new pokemon  snap review janae sitsis wrote fans  clamored for a pokemon snap remake for  years and with new pokemon snap we've  gotten more than we ever bargained for a  great sequel that pulls from all 8  generations of pokemon released so far  dynamic courses that can be explored  during both daytime and night time and  the ability to create an album of edited  personalized pokemon photos which you  can then print or post online a fitting  evolution of the game in the social  media era  after a long gap between titles the  fifth mainline shin megami tensei game  arrived on nintendo's switch this  holiday it's safe to say shin megami  tensei 5 was well worth the wait keeping  up with the traditions of the  long-running franchise shin megami  tensei 5 offered a deep and affecting  jrpg that kept us on our toes throughout  the entire duration of the lengthy  campaign while many jrpgs have a joyful  tone to them shin megami tensei 5 is  relentless in its approach to stick to  dark themes and a brooding atmosphere  its unique style extended to its  turn-based combat which provided some of  the toughest challenges of the year on  nintendo switch the brutal combat system  may have not always felt entirely fair  but there was no denying that it kept us  focused on thinking two steps ahead  despite its dark tones and challenging  combat scenarios shin megami tensor5  still managed to be the most inviting  entry in the series for newcomers due to  its fairly easy to follow story that  doesn't require any knowledge of  previous entries to enjoy with stunning  visuals a story and world that reacted  to your choices and a smartly designed  combat system shin megami tensor5 stood  out as the best jrpg on switch in 2021  in our shin megami tensei 5 review heidi  kemps wrote it's a game that demands a  lot of the player its slow pace and  punishing difficulty will more than  likely turn some folks off but those who  stick with it will find an incredibly  rewarding experience that only gets  better the further in you get shin  megami tensei 5 truly makes you feel  like the weight of this crumbling  conflict-torn world of mythological  nightmares rests firmly on your  shoulders but it's a burden you'll be  glad you chose to bear  [Music]  super mario 3d world certainly wasn't  the first wii u game to get a second  lease on life on nintendo's switch but  it was arguably the most impressive  considering how much it added to the  overall experience nintendo made some  welcome quality of life changes to 3d  world including faster movement speeds  for each character that made the  platforming snappier and a tad more  challenging super mario 3d world is  chock full of awesome content on its own  but this package also added an entirely  new mario experience bowser's fury took  cues from super mario odyssey and  classic mario level design to create an  open world take on the retired plumber's  charming adventures bowser's fury saw  mario team up with bowser jr to stop a  terrifyingly large and furious bowser  from stumping everyone and everything to  bits the open world setting contained a  bunch of gradually unlocking levels with  a unique set of objectives the pleasant  and bright island world was occasionally  disrupted by a dark storm and bowser  spewing fireballs at you while you  frantically tried to collect every last  one of the hundred cat shines plus you  could even travel by water on plessy's  back the package earned a 9 out of 10  and our review said put together super  mario 3d world plus bowser's fury is a  spectacular package super mario 3d world  is an absolute joy of classic  platforming excellence and this is the  best version of it thanks to some well  calibrated improvements  so there you have it gamespot's top 5  nintendo switch exclusives of 2021 we'll  be revealing our top five xbox pc and  playstation games too so make sure you  hit that subscribe button so you can  catch up on the best games of the year  and speaking of we also have a deep dive  into why death loop is our game of the  year thanks so much for watching  [Music]  you
 

